---- Embed overflow and the surveyor unembed (mentor ruling) ----

Landing the allocator overflowed KERNEL_PADDED_SIZE by 3,158
bytes (TIMES value -3158).  Measured, not estimated:
  hardware.fth token stream: 1,579 bytes (HEAD) -> 6,429 bytes
  (green), +4,850.  Pre-registered estimate was 1.5-2KB -- off
  by 2.5x.  METHOD NOTE: measure the comment-stripped token
  stream BEFORE the build next time; the strip pipeline makes
  this a one-liner.

Options on the table, disposition:
  (a) grow KERNEL_PADDED_SIZE 0x1C000 -> 0x1E000: REJECTED --
      would shrink the return stack (which has NO runtime
      overflow check and abuts VAR_STATE with no gap) from
      16.5KB to 12.5KB, and 224 sectors is baked LITERALLY
      into the chainload path (see below), so the G6 iron leg
      would truncate the kernel.
  (fourth) block-loaded companion holding only the free path:
      REJECTED -- the allocator would have two behaviours
      depending on load state, PHYS-AUDIT reporting differently
      in each; the phase-pun species this project was bitten by
      twice in ten days.
  (b) SHIPPED, scoped narrowly: unembed forth/dict/surveyor.fth
      only (20,185 stripped bytes freed vs 3,158 needed).
      Memory map and boot contract untouched.
      embedded.bin: 105,879 -> 85,902 bytes.

KERNEL_SECTORS literal-or-derived (reported either way, per
ruling):
  src/boot/vbr.asm:39   KERNEL_SECTORS equ 224 -- LITERAL, and
      doubly rigid: CHUNK_SECTORS equ 32 with "224 = 7 x 32,
      exact", so 232 would not divide the chunked EDD read.
  forth/dict/install.fth:1060   224 CONSTANT KERNEL-SECTORS --
      LITERAL, but tripwired: test_install.py derives the
      expected value from build/kernel.bin size at runtime and
      goes red on drift.
  A pad growth would therefore have truncated the G6 iron
  chainload silently at boot-medium level; the ruling to leave
  it alone was correct.

Return-stack assert (landed regardless of option, per ruling):
  forth.asm now pins RETURN_STACK_MIN equ 0x4200 and TIMES-
  asserts minimum headroom in ONE direction (shrink refused,
  growth free).  0x4200 = 16,896 bytes = 4,224 nesting levels
  at 4 bytes/cell -- the ENVELOPE figure (today's actual
  headroom), not a measured peak.  Stale forth.asm comment
  ("0x21E00-0x28000", false since the 2026-05-11 pad growth)
  corrected with the reason it was wrong.

